@startuml E3-deployment-01-overview-mvc
title CryptoWeb - Deployment 01: Logical Runtime Overview (MVC)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Client device" as Device <<device>> {
  node "Web browser" as Browser <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "React Views\nAPI client modules" as UI
  }
}
node "Server_3 process :4000" as S3 <<executionEnvironment>> {
  artifact "Express Controllers" as S3Routes
  artifact "Mongoose Models + services" as S3Logic
}
node "Core process :5000" as Core <<executionEnvironment>> {
  artifact "Express Controllers" as CoreRoutes
  artifact "Services + SQL/Mongo data access" as CoreServices
}
node "Python ML process :8000" as ML <<executionEnvironment>> {
  artifact "FastAPI inference handlers" as MLArtifact
}
database "MySQL\nCore SQL schema" as Sql
database "MongoDB\nServer_3: Crypto_data" as MarketMongo
database "MongoDB\nCore: configured DB" as CoreMongo
cloud "Market and news providers" as Providers

Device --> S3 : HTTP/JSON market / orders
Device --> Core : HTTP/JSON identity / wallet
S3 --> Core : HTTP/JSON internal settlement / wallet proxy
Core --> ML : HTTP/JSON predict / anomaly
ML ..> S3 : optional feature-data API
S3 --> MarketMongo : Mongoose
Core --> Sql : MySQL client
Core --> CoreMongo : native Mongo driver
S3 --> Providers : HTTPS / WSS / RSS
Core --> Providers : HTTPS price quotes

legend bottom
Runtime/process topology - not a claim that each process runs on a separate physical host.
Core and Server_3 MongoDB names are distinct logical databases; host placement is configurable.
External TLS and reverse-proxy deployment details are unspecified by the repository.
endlegend

@enduml
